# AGV onboard HMI machines.
# Managed by 8005-workspace\remote-ops\onboard-hmi. See that README for the full design.
#
# Each car sits behind its own KonNaD CPE2458 doing NAT. We reach the HMI by
# port-forwarding an external port on the CPE's enterprise-LAN address to the
# HMI's port 22. External 22 is NOT usable: the CPE's own dropbear owns it.

Host agv*
    User agvops
    IdentityFile C:\Users\szy\.ssh\agv_ops_ed25519
    IdentitiesOnly yes
    # These machines are freshly imaged and their host keys are unknown on first
    # contact. accept-new records the key on first connect and refuses it if it
    # ever changes afterwards -- unlike `no`, which would ignore changes forever.
    StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new
    ConnectTimeout 10
    # The link is wireless via CPE; keep dead sessions from hanging forever.
    ServerAliveInterval 30
    ServerAliveCountMax 3

# Car 1 -- DESKTOP-94OA6CK, HMI LAN 192.168.71.180
# 22022 chosen because the CPE already forwards 80, 443, 502, 2222, 5001-5003,
# 5010, 5900, 8001, 8005, 8008, 8009, and owns 22 itself (dropbear).
Host agv01
    HostName 172.19.162.210
    Port 22022

# Car 2 -- CPE at 172.19.162.179. Same model as car 1's: SSH-2.0-dropbear on 22,
# web UI on 80, measured 2026-09-03 from the control host over the direct Wi-Fi
# subnet (Find-NetRoute said Wi-Fi, not Clash, so the probe is real).
#
# Also 22022, same as car 1. The two CPEs are separate devices reached by
# separate addresses, so the external port never had to differ -- one number for
# every car is easier to remember than a per-car increment.
#
# Verified 2026-09-03: agvops@DESKTOP-94OA6CK, pwsh 7.6.5, Windows 10 Pro.
#
# That COMPUTERNAME is car 1's too. The two are different physical machines
# (different MAC, different SSH host key, different uptime) cloned from one
# image with nothing re-personalized: same COMPUTERNAME, same MachineGuid
# 6910ff68-24ae-4fcb-8e16-b6bbd5924490, same SMBIOS UUID, same InstallDate, and
# the same 192.168.71.180 on their own NATed LANs. So the ALIAS is the only
# thing that tells the cars apart from here -- never key anything off the
# machine name or MachineGuid.
Host agv02
    HostName 172.19.162.179
    Port 22022

# Car 3 -- CPE at 172.19.162.70, forwarding 22022 to 192.168.71.180:22. That
# LAN address is the same as cars 1 and 2: all three are clones of one image and
# each sits behind its own CPE's NAT, so the collision is confined and harmless.
#
# Probed 2026-09-03 from the control host over the direct Wi-Fi subnet: 22 is the
# CPE's own dropbear, 80 its web UI, and 22022 is REFUSED -- the forward exists
# but the HMI has no sshd yet. Same state agv02 was in before docs/USAGE.md
# section 7 steps 2-3 were run on it over VNC.
Host agv03
    HostName 172.19.162.70
    Port 22022
